# Line endings: LF, everywhere, on every platform.
#
# The committed files are already LF. These rules only stop a checkout from
# changing them (core.autocrlf=true on Windows would expand LF to CRLF). The
# vendored crate folders record a checksum for every file, and cargo refuses to
# build from a crate whose files no longer match, so a checkout that rewrote
# line endings would break every vendored build.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never touched. A binary file with newline translation applied to it is
# silently corrupt, so these are declared rather than left to git's heuristic.
*.png    binary
*.nupkg  binary
*.dylib  binary
*.so     binary
*.dll    binary
*.pdb    binary
*.xz     binary
*.gz     binary
*.zip    binary
*.crate  binary
*.wasm   binary
*.a      binary
*.lib    binary
*.o      binary
*.ico    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.gif    binary
*.ttf    binary
*.woff   binary
*.woff2  binary

# The vendored crate folders and the tool sources are byte-for-byte copies of what crates.io
# published (the dioxus-cli source with the recorded patches applied); every vendored file has a
# recorded checksum, and the patch check compares the tool sources byte for byte. Git must not
# normalise their line endings (some upstream files are CRLF) or cargo will refuse to build from
# them.
src/CodeBrix.WebPlatform.FrontendBuilder/Rust/vendor/**   -text
tools/dx-native-tools/sources/**                          -text
